                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7e595e0c-86c4-46d3-a971-880aaa6487aa",
                        "source_entry_id": "50c60024-2990-3dda-be42-0484bab8e84a",
                        "source_sense_id": "c1cf962d-9030-3019-9716-c30967bd65e5",
                        "source_sense_description": "gehoben: eine Folgerung einleitend: folglich, also",
                        "target_lang_word": "consequently",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "consequently",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "60a147e1-e5d4-3bc1-9ae0-3e4c3994824c",
                                        "entry_id": "a7e4297a-c2b0-371b-b476-33dd5894e276",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "As a result or consequence of something; subsequently."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "conjunctive",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cde5d261-5852-4c1e-aeb1-98ccea7ea6ac",
                                                "sense_id": "60a147e1-e5d4-3bc1-9ae0-3e4c3994824c",
                                                "text": "He didn't wake up early. Consequently, he was late to work."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5999f517-6b1d-494a-983d-826c4e1bb49a",
                                                "sense_id": "60a147e1-e5d4-3bc1-9ae0-3e4c3994824c",
                                                "text": "He Suſpends on theſe Reaſons, that Thomas Rue had granted a general Diſcharge to Adam Muſhet, who was his Conjunct, and correus debendi, after the alleadged Service, which Diſcharged Muſhet, and conſequently Houstoun his Partner."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d4594b5-1496-4937-b404-bf2a3fee43d7",
                                                "sense_id": "60a147e1-e5d4-3bc1-9ae0-3e4c3994824c",
                                                "text": "While algebraical reasoning is most frequently analytical, arithmetical reasoning is generally synthetical, and, consequently, more difficult to understand."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ce4bf89f-9308-3f63-bdd9-8542ff7b5d6a",
                                        "entry_id": "a7e4297a-c2b0-371b-b476-33dd5894e276",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "subsequently, following after in time or sequence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "sequence"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "105ad0fb-4714-47d7-b2f3-beaac6f462ca",
                        "source_entry_id": "50c60024-2990-3dda-be42-0484bab8e84a",
                        "source_sense_id": "c1cf962d-9030-3019-9716-c30967bd65e5",
                        "source_sense_description": "gehoben: eine Folgerung einleitend: folglich, also",
                        "target_lang_word": "therefore",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "therefore",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d5e39bb3-46ac-3429-9607-b48e87449b18",
                                        "entry_id": "dfe4845c-c283-3473-b130-6369e1ea8935",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Consequently, by or in consequence of that or this cause; referring to something previously stated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "conjunctive",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40fbf13c-cc31-47d7-806b-6082eb0202d9",
                                                "sense_id": "d5e39bb3-46ac-3429-9607-b48e87449b18",
                                                "text": "Traditional values will always have a place—therefore, they will never lose relevance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22f9500b-699f-476c-b3b5-d34d86fc9150",
                                                "sense_id": "d5e39bb3-46ac-3429-9607-b48e87449b18",
                                                "text": "I've been explicitly forbidden to leave and therefore must stay longer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04756caf-c792-423c-8861-8f44559bd973",
                                                "sense_id": "d5e39bb3-46ac-3429-9607-b48e87449b18",
                                                "text": "I left the office at 5 o'clock. I was therefore not there when the fire started a quarter of an hour later."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34821ae0-beb5-4463-8426-8a75d84efa86",
                                                "sense_id": "d5e39bb3-46ac-3429-9607-b48e87449b18",
                                                "text": "I have married a wife, and therefore I can not come."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db9c1fc7-05e9-44c6-ba04-91b1bc88e91b",
                                                "sense_id": "d5e39bb3-46ac-3429-9607-b48e87449b18",
                                                "text": "Je pense, donc je suis (I think, therefore I am)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9c74313-de9b-4036-9e6b-e7e870b9eb8b",
                                                "sense_id": "d5e39bb3-46ac-3429-9607-b48e87449b18",
                                                "text": "In the old days, to my commonplace and unobserving mind, he gave no evidences of genius whatsoever. He never read me any of his manuscripts, […], and therefore my lack of detection of his promise may in some degree be pardoned."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "026260e6-ab62-4f9b-9d70-58e6897be38b",
                                                "sense_id": "d5e39bb3-46ac-3429-9607-b48e87449b18",
                                                "text": "Creating a complete map of the human connectome would therefore be a monumental milestone but not the end of the journey to understanding how our brains work."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d6442df-21d4-4bea-b78b-ffe4a6a9468b",
                                                "sense_id": "d5e39bb3-46ac-3429-9607-b48e87449b18",
                                                "text": "He blushes; therefore he is innocent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "643be500-cd4b-3d4e-81a0-8fafa6358794",
                                        "entry_id": "dfe4845c-c283-3473-b130-6369e1ea8935",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "for that; for it (in reference to a previous statement)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "conjunctive",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1190b7a3-60b3-48fc-83ab-dbd453e9c927",
                                                "sense_id": "643be500-cd4b-3d4e-81a0-8fafa6358794",
                                                "text": "Behold, we have forsaken all, and followed thee; what shall we have therefore?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "69c072fd-667b-45d7-8a82-b9796fe0f613",
                        "source_entry_id": "50c60024-2990-3dda-be42-0484bab8e84a",
                        "source_sense_id": "c1cf962d-9030-3019-9716-c30967bd65e5",
                        "source_sense_description": "gehoben: eine Folgerung einleitend: folglich, also",
                        "target_lang_word": "thus",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "thus",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1eb5bb97-1f83-338c-a7f1-3c18ded2efb1",
                                        "entry_id": "7dac3729-2c53-3feb-908d-ac5eb7187ca6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In this way or manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "formal",
                                            "literary",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "964e18eb-f5f4-477c-9531-529e0893a69c",
                                                "sense_id": "1eb5bb97-1f83-338c-a7f1-3c18ded2efb1",
                                                "text": "If you throw the ball thus, as I’m showing you, you’ll have better luck hitting the target."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28c4aea7-e604-4c7a-b748-8c11104eb00d",
                                                "sense_id": "1eb5bb97-1f83-338c-a7f1-3c18ded2efb1",
                                                "text": "But then I had the [massive] flintlock by me for protection. ¶[…]The linen-press and a chest on the top of it formed, however, a very good gun-carriage; and, thus mounted, aim could be taken out of the window at the old mare feeding in the meadow below by the brook, and a 'bead' could be drawn upon Molly, the dairymaid, kissing the fogger behind the hedge,[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "724f4d1d-2155-4e7c-97a0-37493b0b218d",
                                                "sense_id": "1eb5bb97-1f83-338c-a7f1-3c18ded2efb1",
                                                "text": "David Mason, Beverage and Bar Manager at St. Regis, describes the complex aromas and layered palate of the cognac thus: “It’s kind of autumn flavors. Really nutty, almondy – kind of fig, plum, dried fruits. But it finishes off really smoothly but with a little bit of tobacco leaf.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e64824d-9475-37c1-b9b5-4c3a9ef81a2e",
                                        "entry_id": "7dac3729-2c53-3feb-908d-ac5eb7187ca6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "As a result."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "conjunctive",
                                            "formal",
                                            "literary",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a4fc2aa-0326-4727-b70f-07b730361bdd",
                                                "sense_id": "9e64824d-9475-37c1-b9b5-4c3a9ef81a2e",
                                                "text": "I have all the tools I need; thus, I will be able to fix the car without having to call a mechanic."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "266e74e2-778c-4129-b761-9fc441faa324",
                                                "sense_id": "9e64824d-9475-37c1-b9b5-4c3a9ef81a2e",
                                                "text": "I corralled the judge, and we started off across the fields, in no very mild state of fear of that gentleman's wife, whose vigilance was seldom relaxed. And thus we came by a circuitous route to Mohair, the judge occupied by his own guilty thoughts, and I by others not less disturbing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00312c4d-3007-4a30-9f4f-7cb0a318ab03",
                                                "sense_id": "9e64824d-9475-37c1-b9b5-4c3a9ef81a2e",
                                                "text": "Not unnaturally, “Auntie” took this communication in bad part. Thus outraged, she showed herself to be a bold as well as a furious virago."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4816e199-2ac9-406e-8170-04b5ebebd0b1",
                                                "sense_id": "9e64824d-9475-37c1-b9b5-4c3a9ef81a2e",
                                                "text": "[The researchers] noticed many of their pieces of [plastic marine] debris sported surface pits around two microns across. Such pits are about the size of a bacterial cell. Closer examination showed that some of these pits did, indeed, contain bacteria, and that in several cases these bacteria were dividing and thus, by the perverse arithmetic of biological terminology, multiplying."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
